.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH crisk-compile 1  "compile 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
crisk\-compile \- Compile the tier policy into acc\*(Aqs tier section, a requirements document or prose
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcrisk compile\fR [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-policy\fR] [\fB\-\-map\fR] [\fB\-\-base\fR] [\fB\-\-checkout\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fB\-\-to\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Compile the tier policy into acc\*(Aqs tier section, a requirements document or prose
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress status lines on stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-to\fR \fI<TO>\fR
What to produce
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
acc: agent\-change\-control\*(Aqs `tiers` and `missing_tier` policy section (YAML)
.IP \(bu 2
requirements: The tool\-neutral requirements document (JSON)
.IP \(bu 2
prose: The policy as Markdown, for people and auditors
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-policy\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
The policy file; without it, the policy is read from \-\-base
.TP
\fB\-\-map\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
The map file, with \-\-policy
.TP
\fB\-\-base\fR \fI<REV>\fR
Read .change\-risk/ at this revision of \-\-checkout (default HEAD)
.TP
\fB\-\-checkout\fR \fI<DIR>\fR [default: .]

.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Write to FILE instead of stdout
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
